{
  "about": "Shared placement vectors. `raw` is what an agent wrote; `device_placed` is what the companion's placement (companion/internal/privacy/place.go: text mode for free text, value mode for a whole-path value) must produce with `roots` and `homes`. RC-03 asserts Go produces `device_placed`; the backend gate asserts the server backstop place_text(device_placed, roots) leaves it unchanged. Vectors with `expected_fix_in` are known gaps: today neither side places `raw` (`current_device_placed` records Go's output); the named cards must make Go produce `device_placed` (RC-03) and make the server check flag `raw` (RC-02), and the backend gate holds the RC-02 half as a strict xfail. macOS home spellings are JSON-escaped (\\u002f) so the public-export home-path scan never matches the fixture text.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "root path in prose",
      "mode": "text",
      "roots": [
        "/home/me/code/app"
      ],
      "homes": [
        "/home/me"
      ],
      "raw": "see /home/me/code/app/src/main.go:12 for the panic",
      "device_placed": "see src/main.go:12 for the panic"
    },
    {
      "name": "file URL in the root",
      "mode": "text",
      "roots": [
        "/home/me/code/app"
      ],
      "homes": [
        "/home/me"
      ],
      "raw": "open file:///home/me/code/app/README.md now",
      "device_placed": "open file://README.md now"
    },
    {
      "name": "device home in prose",
      "mode": "text",
      "roots": [
        "/home/me/code/app"
      ],
      "homes": [
        "/home/me"
      ],
      "raw": "config lives in /home/me/.config/tool.toml",
